driver — what drives what

  driver                 the bindings
  driver stop <name>     stop a standalone driver process
  driver start <name>    start it again
  driver rescan          read the manifests again, bind anything new

The device manager matches hardware to drivers and is the only thing
that knows vendor numbers. A manifest in /lib/drivers names the
hardware it fits and where its driver lives: a program the manager
starts, or a service that comes and claims the assignment. A driver
belonging to a service has no process of its own, so it cannot be
stopped here; its service owns it.

Dropping a manifest and its program into /lib/drivers and running
`driver rescan` brings a new driver up on a running machine.
